## Tier 2 (on demand)

`jaxfne-api-truth`, `jaxfne-code-orientation`, `jaxfne-test-runner`, `jaxfne-repo-audit`, `jaxfne-evidence-validator`, `jaxfne-style-conformance`, `jaxfne-tutorial-executor`, `jaxfne-theta-tutorial-validator`, `jaxfne-worker-handoff`, `jaxfne-jax-lint`, `jaxfne-visualization-schema`, `jaxfne-sha256-artifact-integrity` — see `internal_docs/skills/adapters/`.

## Workflow

1. Match task to a skill trigger.
2. Read the repo super-skill or adapter file.
3. If a user-installed skill with the same name is loaded, follow it.
4. Before reporting success on tutorial/release work, satisfy `jaxfne-notebook-release-gate` or `jaxfne-evidence-validator` gates.
5. Before remote mutation, apply `jaxfne-release-mutation-guard`.

## Local full skills (optional, never committed)

Developers may symlink user-installed skills into `.cursor/skills/` or `.cursor/local/` locally. Both paths are gitignored.
